# Ignored by default, same spirit as *.docx/*.md above: anything dropped
# into tests/ (scratch fixtures, one-off files) stays untracked unless
# force-added, so `git add -A` can't sweep in something new by accident.
# Unlike the *.docx/*.md patterns above, a directory-level ignore can't be
# selectively un-ignored per file (git won't re-include a path whose parent
# directory is excluded) — already-tracked files under tests/ (parse_testing.rs,
# the *.docx fixtures and their exceptions above, fixtures/settings.conf) are
# unaffected, since gitignore never hides an already-tracked file. A new
# deliberate fixture needs `git add -f path/to/it` instead of a `!` exception.
tests/

# Added by cargo

/target
